1785544567268214	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy6gQ		item.comment	bn-v1c	{"body":"SD-09 paid. Absorbed the §4.5/§4.6/§4.7 operational contract into the four owning documents (RFC-2119 throughout), commit df59617 in .maw/workspaces/bn-v1c.\n\ndocs/35 (daemon): scheduling/priority classes + memory budget (§4.1 tail, named in the old banner); crash-safe publication ordering, restart binary (resume-from-committed-continuation | Failed with typed reason), fsck with three typed defect classes; storage lifecycle — GC roots, per-class store layout grounded in crates/continuum-workspace/src/artifact_path.rs, campaign summarization with normative ordering (certificate attested by a kernel-covenant checker before raw results become collectable); purge and the Redacted stub incl. closed reason vocabulary table and audit obligation; backup and verified restore; identity/capabilities/cross-principal sharing with the existence-oracle rules; two-epoch migration duties; engine-defect lifecycle; telemetry-never-inside-evidence.\n\nRFC 0026 (wire slice only, kept scoped — general expansion is bn-1bf): new 'Operational contract on the wire' section (Redacted values, publication/quota/storage failure, existence oracles incl. per-actor idempotency-key probing, epoch advance, engine defects); capability secrecy bullet in Transport; sharpened the capability-administration open question (audit obligation is not conditional on closing the registry gap); four acceptance-test families added.\n\nADR-0018: rewritten around six independently versioned epochs, four advance obligations, ordering rationale (five of six have no Ord; protocol does), and what is not an epoch.\n\ndocs/42: epoch-advance→reuse table, redacted/summarized/collected inputs vs reuse classes, parity mismatches emit defect_*.\n\nCorrections with direction (recorded in-document): [docs/35] GC root set widened to include live tasks (plan §4.5 → docs/35); §4.5 storage lifecycle scoped to content-addressed classes, cap_* governed by revoke not purge (plan §4.5 → docs/35); Redacted's normative form is four fields (schemas/IDL → docs/35); engine identity is not a seventh epoch (plan §4.7 → docs/35, ADR-0018). [ADR-0018] pre-R3 version list replaced by the six epochs (docs/12 §7, RFC 0026, epoch.rs → ADR-0018); compatibility statement MUST be published *before* the advance is applied (plan §4.6 → ADR-0018, tightened). [docs/42] parity mismatch emits defect_* as well as a counterexample (plan §4.7 → docs/42); retention MUST NOT collect an input the promotion lane still needs, and an unrunnable audit is typed-inconclusive, never a pass (plan §4.5 → docs/42, ordered).\n\nplan §25 ledger: 'SD-09 (open)' → 'SD-09 (paid, PR 0)' with the per-document split appended; only that line touched. Traceability regenerated (SD-09 now status:satisfied, ledger_status:'paid, PR 0'). validate_dossier.py: \"status\": \"pass\", program_status ready, spec_debt open=[SD-10]. validation-results.json / VALIDATION_REPORT.md untouched."}	blake3:Jm2DCqCQNEvOmoERxaQqwGP_9zPjVEroUxZeLCScAVM
